test_symlink — exercise TFS-v2's S_IFLNK symlink primitive
============================================================

Phase 0e (symlink piece): TFS gained `S_IFLNK = 5` plus `tfs_symlink`
and `tfs_readlink`. Symlinks store their target as inline file data
(reusing the file write/read path), and TFS does NOT auto-follow
them — `tfs_lookup` returns the symlink's own inode unchanged. A
real POSIX symlink layer (auto-follow at `open()` time) lands in
the shim later if needed.

This test covers the two primitive operations through the FS server:

  1. `symlink("/some/target", "/tmp/lnk_a")` — creates the link.
  2. `readlink("/tmp/lnk_a", buf)` — reads the target back; must
     match what was written byte-for-byte.
  3. Re-`readlink` after a second `open` to confirm the data block
     is durable across opens.
  4. `readlink` of a non-symlink path (the test binary itself,
     `/bin/test_symlink`) must return -1 — proves the type check
     in `tfs_readlink` actually fires.

Pass: prints `symlink: ok`. Failure prints `symlink: bad N` where
N tags the failing step.

    module oskit.bin.test_symlink

    import oskit.ulib.{puts, exit, exit_with, symlink, readlink}


    print_idec(v: int)
        var n = v
        if n < 0
            puts("-")
            n = -n
        if n >= 10
            print_idec(n / 10)
        var b: [1]byte
        b[0] = byte('0' + (n % 10))
        puts(string(&b[0], 1))


    fail(code: int)
        puts("symlink: bad ")
        print_idec(code)
        puts("\n")
        exit_with(code)


    main(argv: []string)
        val target = "/etc/passwd"
        val link = "/tmp/lnk_phase0e"

        if symlink(target, link) != 0
            fail(1)
            return

        var buf: [64]byte
        val n = readlink(link, &buf[0], 64)
        if n != 11
            fail(2)
            return

The target is "/etc/passwd" (11 bytes). Verify the bytes round-trip
intact — a typo in the wire format or in `tfs_write`/`tfs_read`'s
inline-data path would corrupt the readback.

        val expected = "/etc/passwd"
        val ep = *byte(expected)
        var i = 0
        while i < 11
            if buf[i] != ep[i]
                fail(3)
                return
            i += 1

A second readlink on the same link must produce identical bytes.
Catches bugs where the data block is consumed/freed by the first
read.

        var buf2: [64]byte
        val n2 = readlink(link, &buf2[0], 64)
        if n2 != 11
            fail(4)
            return
        i = 0
        while i < 11
            if buf2[i] != ep[i]
                fail(5)
                return
            i += 1

readlink on a non-symlink must reject. /bin/test_symlink is the
running binary itself — guaranteed to be a regular file.

        var b3: [16]byte
        val r = readlink("/bin/test_symlink", &b3[0], 16)
        if r != -1
            fail(6)
            return

        puts("symlink: ok\n")
        exit()
